Port Mapping/Port Expose:
----------------------------

Container don't have Public IP addresses. They have ports.
EC2 machine have IP addresses. What we will do we will take one port from EC2 and one port from Container and map both of them and open the port
By using Base Machine(EC2) IP addresses. The request will go to Base Machine(EC2) through port because we have mapped.
With the help of Base Machine Port we are exposing the Container Port to the outside world. That's why it is called port mapping
We do this because Container don't have any IP addresses.

docker run -td --name webcont1 -p 8081:80 ubuntu /bin/bash   # -td: Runs the container in detached mode, meaning it runs in the background
                                                             # --name webcont1: Assigns the name webcont1 to the container.
												             # -p 8081:80: Maps port 8081 on the host machine to port 80 inside the container. Traffic sent to
												                http://<host-ip>:8081 is forwarded to port 80 in the container.
													 
docker exec -it webcont1 /bin/bash                           # It is used to open a Bash shell inside an already running Docker container.
                                                             # docker exec: Executes a command inside an existing, running container.
															 # webcont1: The name (or ID) of the running container.
															 # /bin/bash: Starts the Bash shell inside the container.

